n\n<p>But we have 2.4 moles. So, Cr<sub>2</sub>(SO<sub>4</sub>)<sub>3</sub> is excess reagent and Pb(NO<sub>3</sub>)<sub>2</sub> is limiting reagent, (LR)</p>\n\n<img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l42qhbq6/d44e434f-b07a-469a-a3f6-e984abf1e566/9bf1cbe0-e597-11ec-8082-a116589b2e55/file-1l42qhbq7.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l42qhbq6/d44e434f-b07a-469a-a3f6-e984abf1e566/9bf1cbe0-e597-11ec-8082-a116589b2e55/file-1l42qhbq7.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"JEE Main 2021 (Online) 16th March Evening Shift Chemistry - Some Basic Concepts of Chemistry Question 168 English Explanation 2\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l42qhbq6/d44e434f-b07a-469a-a3f6-e984abf1e566/9bf1cbe0-e597-11ec-8082-a116589b2e55/file-1l42qhbq7.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l42qhbq6/d44e434f-b07a-469a-a3f6-e984abf1e566/9bf1cbe0-e597-11ec-8082-a116589b2e55/file-1l42qhbq7.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l42qhbq6/d44e434f-b07a-469a-a3f6-e984abf1e566/9bf1cbe0-e597-11ec-8082-a116589b2e55/file-1l42qhbq7.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1l42qhbq6/d44e434f-b07a-469a-a3f6-e984abf1e566/9bf1cbe0-e597-11ec-8082-a116589b2e55/file-1l42qhbq7.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1l42qhbq6/d44e434f-b07a-469a-a3f6-e984abf1e566/9bf1cbe0-e597-11ec-8082-a116589b2e55/file-1l42qhbq7.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1l42qhbq6/d44e434f-b07a-469a-a3f6-e984abf1e566/9bf1cbe0-e597-11ec-8082-a116589b2e55/file-1l42qhbq7.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\">\n\n <p>Moles of PbSO<sub>4</sub> formed = moles of Pb(NO<sub>3</sub>)<sub>2</sub> consumed\n\n\n<br><br>= 5.25 m mol = 525 <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" 